{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_column_varcoeff_faceflux_forced",
    "description": "MMS driver for the free-name-free flux-form operator d/dz(K du/dz - F): u_t = d/dz(K du/dz - F) + S(z,t) on the unit column [0, 1], K(z) = 1 + z supplied on the NLEV+1 interfaces (K[kn] = 1 + ze[kn]) and a PRESCRIBED upward interface flux F(z) = gamma exp(z / zscale) (F[kn] = gamma exp(ze[kn] / zscale), gamma = 0.3, zscale = 1 m), discretized on the quadratic-stretch column by grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev. Manufactured solution u(z,t) = exp(-t) cos(pi z) as in problems/heat_column_varcoeff_forced: the forcing that makes it exact is that problem's S plus dF/dz = (gamma / zscale) exp(z / zscale), i.e. S(z,t) = exp(-t) [ -cos(pi z) + pi sin(pi z) + pi^2 (1+z) cos(pi z) ] + (gamma / zscale) exp(z / zscale), evaluated at the layer centres zc (a RUNTIME position) and the ODE time t. K u_z vanishes at both ends (sin(0) = sin(pi) = 0), so the exact total flux through each domain face is -F there, which is precisely the rule's face closure. F is chosen so the case exercises every F path of the rule: it is NONZERO at both faces (F[1] = gamma, F[NLEV+1] = gamma e), so dropping, sign-flipping or mis-indexing either face term leaves an O(1/dz) error in a boundary layer; and it is CURVED and non-polynomial, so the interior difference (F[k+1] - F[k]) / dz[k] is only a second-order approximation of dF/dz(zc) and an index shift in it shows as a first-order error. The recorded errors therefore differ from heat_column_varcoeff_forced's: the t = 0.1 error is the combined second-order spatial error of the K and F parts on a stretched mesh. The mesh follows the grid's edge-array contract (ze taken from the grid's shared MMS test column mms_column_ze in grids/column_nonuniform_1d/mesh/mms_column.esm; zc/dz grid-derived); build-time ic/reference positions spell the layer centre from literals and NLEV, because neither the free-name zc observed nor an expression template resolves there (AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "equation:heat",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev.esm"
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/column_nonuniform_1d/mesh/mms_column.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Temperature over the lev (layer) axis."
        },
        "K": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Interface diffusivity K = 1 + z evaluated on the interfaces, K[kn] = 1 + ze[kn]."
        },
        "F": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K m/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Prescribed upward interface flux F = gamma exp(z / zscale) on the interfaces, F[kn] = gamma exp(ze[kn] / zscale) (F[1] = gamma at the surface, F[NLEV+1] = gamma e at the top with zscale = 1 m), differentiated together with the diffusive flux by the rule."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Manufactured forcing S(zc, t) = exp(-t) [ -cos(pi zc) + pi sin(pi zc) + pi^2 (1 + zc) cos(pi zc) ] + (gamma / zscale) exp(zc / zscale)."
        },
        "gamma": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K m/s",
          "default": 0.3,
          "description": "Amplitude of the prescribed interface flux F = gamma exp(z / zscale); the forcing cancels its divergence (gamma / zscale) exp(z / zscale)."
        },
        "zscale": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Length scale of the prescribed flux, F = gamma exp(z / zscale), keeping the exponent dimensionless."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Interface coordinates of the quadratic-stretch column, the grid's shared MMS test column mms_column_ze (grids/column_nonuniform_1d/mesh/mms_column.esm): ze[kn] = 0.6 ((kn-1)/NLEV) + 0.4 ((kn-1)/NLEV)^2 for kn = 1..NLEV+1 (ze[1] = 0 the surface, ze[NLEV+1] = 1 the top), the single geometry input of the grid's edge-array contract, spelled in the library from the metaparameter name NLEV so a loader-API rebinding re-derives the whole mesh."
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer centres, GRID-DERIVED from ze by applying grids/column_nonuniform_1d column_cell_center. Read by the rules by bare name."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thicknesses, GRID-DERIVED from ze by applying column_cell_thickness. The finite-volume measure read by the rules by bare name."
        }
      },
